\DOC WITH_GOAL

\TYPE {WITH_GOAL : (term -> tactic) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
{WITH_GOAL tac} runs the tactic that {tac} computes from the current goal's
conclusion, so the tactic applied is selected by the conclusion itself.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {tac : term -> tactic} maps the goal's conclusion to a tactic.
Given a goal with conclusion {t}, the conclusion is passed to {tac} and the
resulting tactic is applied to that same goal, yielding whatever that tactic
yields. In the observed traces the outcome is one of: the goal is closed (zero
subgoals); the conclusion is replaced by a rewritten or beta-reduced one, i.e.
{
   ?- t
   ========================  WITH_GOAL tac
   ?- u
}
\noindent or the goal is split into two subgoals whose conclusions are branches
extracted from {t}. No observed trace has any assumptions present, so only the
conclusion is seen to change.

\COMMENTS
The observed inputs are all goals with no assumptions whose conclusions have
one similar shape, and the argument functions dispatch on the syntactic form of
the conclusion.

\ENDDOC
